    It is always preferred to use :func:`~solve` when possible, as it is faster and more
    numerically stable than computing :math:`A^{-n}` explicitly.

.. seealso::

        :func:`torch.linalg.solve` computes :attr:`A`\ `.inverse() @ \ `:attr:`B` with a
